                    </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>percent_coverage</name>
                    <field_number>9</field_number>
                    <field_location unit="byte">329</field_location>
                    <data_type>ASCII_Real</data_type>
                    <field_length unit="byte">7</field_length>
                    <description>
                        The percentage coverage of all longitudes in the product.
                    </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>rings:minimum_corotating_ring_longitude</name>
                    <field_number>10</field_number>
                    <field_location unit="byte">337</field_location>
                    <data_type>ASCII_Real</data_type>
                    <field_length unit="byte">6</field_length>
                    <unit>deg</unit>
                    <description>
                        The lower end of the range of co-rotating longitude that contains
                        valid data. Note that this is not always the same quantity as the
                        rings:minimum_corotating_ring_longitude of the product label: a
                        mosaic label reports the full grid, 0 to 359.98 degrees, because a
                        mosaic is always written out to its full extent. When the range of
                        valid data wraps through 360 degrees this value is greater than
                        the maximum.
                    </description>
                </Field_Character>
                <Field_Character>
                    <name>rings:maximum_corotating_ring_longitude</name>
                    <field_number>11</field_number>
                    <field_location unit="byte">344</field_location>
                    <data_type>ASCII_Real</data_type>
                    <field_length unit="byte">6</field_length>
                    <unit>deg</unit>
                    <description>
                        The upper end of the range of co-rotating longitude that contains
                        valid data. Note that this is not always the same quantity as the
                        rings:maximum_corotating_ring_longitude of the product label: a
                        mosaic label reports the full grid, 0 to 359.98 degrees, because a
                        mosaic is always written out to its full extent. When the range of
                        valid data wraps through 360 degrees this value is less than the
                        minimum.
                    </description>
                </Field_Character>
